hadiths[1]{hadithnumber,text}:
"1310","We are Bundar, we are Abu Amer, we are Abu Mawdud, and he is Abd al-Aziz bin Abi Suleiman. Abd al-Rahman bin Abi Hadrad told me. Al-Aslami said: I heard Abu Hurairah saying: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Whoever enters this mosque and spits in it or “It sneezes, let him dig in it, put it away, let him bury it. If he does not do that, let him spit in his garment, then bring it out.”"
